      "id": "inside-out-reciprocals",
      "title": "Evaluate the nested reciprocals",
      "explanation": "An exponent of \\(-1\\) means take the reciprocal, so work from the innermost parentheses outward. Starting with \\(2+1=3\\), the successive steps are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^{-1}+1&=\\frac13+1=\\frac43,\\\\\n\\left(\\frac43\\right)^{-1}+1&=\\frac34+1=\\frac74,\\\\\n\\left(\\frac74\\right)^{-1}+1&=\\frac47+1=\\boxed{\\frac{11}{7}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is choice B.",
